Debugging Flow in Selenium
Test Execution
      ↓
Test Fails
      ↓
Read Error Message
      ↓
Identify Failure Point
      ↓
Analyze Root Cause
      ↓
Fix Script/Application
      ↓
Re-run Test
      ↓
Verify Result

Common Selenium Errors
A. NoSuchElementException--->driver.find_element(By.ID, "username123")|
                                                                    |
 solution -> WebDriverWait(driver,10).until(
    EC.presence_of_element_located((By.ID,"username"))
) 

B.  TimeoutException
problem -
 WebDriverWait(driver,5).until(
    EC.visibility_of_element_located((By.ID,"login"))
)
solution - WebDriverWait(driver,15)

c. StaleElementRefrenceException 
problem - page refreshed after element locating 
button.click()
driver.refresh()

button.click()
-------------------------------------------------------------
BreakPoint -A breakpoint pauses execution at a specific line.
example -
       driver.get("hhtps://google.com")
       search_box = driver.find_element(BY.NAME , "q") <-breakpoint
       send_keys("python")
   

Debugging Tech -
1) Print statement --  print("step 1") 
                  driver.get("https://google.com")
                       print("setp 2)
                  x = driver.find_element(By.NAME , "x")
                       print("step 3)
                       send_keys("hello")
2) Logging --- 
         import Logging
         Logging.baseConfig(level= logging.info)
         logging.info("LoggingInfo")

3) ScreentShot 
         driver.save_screenshot("debug.png")

4) Browser Inspection
         crtl+ shift + i 
         F12
         right click menu->inspect                   
5) Explicit Wait
         WebDriverWait(driver,10).until(
    EC.visibility_of_element_located((By.ID,"login"))
    )
